From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-cuda: E4M3 latent caches on KV pages - the fp8+pages marriage (Mia 1104 0017-0025, adapted to v1.2.3)

PROVENANCE: ported from MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104,
patches/engine/0017-0025 (Apache-2.0, (c) MiaAI Lab) against TensorFold
00e7ddd (v1.2.2), 2026-11-05, by this line. SCOPE: the marriage only -
their 0026-0033 (the EXL3 load-ahead, the MoE-glue fusion, the step-link
work) are separate optimizations, not ported. ADAPTATION: per-patch
scratch commits; the fetch kernels rewritten onto v1.2.2 restructured
load_kv (the byte-wise E4M3 decode; the dense chunk loads as the window
with bases moved once - 0023 superseding 0017 per-key form); the KV_HOST
branches preserved (pkPageBytes, the 6-arg addCache, the p.pk pooled-keys
pages); stateSizes keeps our 5-param signature (the fixed part holds no
head-conditional rows on this tree); cuda.zig/cuda_start/cuda_native/
cuda_pages/snapshot_layout adapted to our shapes; the registry records
appended to our import lists. **0022's Table.logical extended to ALL
THREE latent.Table sites on v1.2.2 (their base had one)** - the TokenUnits
contract in chunks() demands t.logical == paged8 at every paged sparse
call, and 0021's dispatch routes E4M3 to the _paged kernels at every
site; the one-site port died at the first DSA sparse launch (both ranks,
campaign-20261105-105143 - the receipt). SEMANTICS: TF_KV_PAGES=on pages
either format (one shared pool, 6,380 bytes/token E4M3 beside DFlash2 vs
13,056 bf16), unknown values refused (BadKvPages), the pool admits
elastically (PoolTooSmall), every mapped page id checked on every rank
(BadStep). The unpaged standing config is preserved by construction (the
flags default off; pageBytesOf(false,true) = the old pageBytes).
OWNER: this line; STATUS: EXPERIMENTAL, judged by the fp8-pages window
(the boot pool shape, the gates, the instruments). Mia original reasoning
follows.

STAGING: applies AFTER glm-mia-absorb-mma.patch (alphabetical:
absorb-mma < fp8-pages). The cuda_glue.zig Kernels hunks re-anchored onto
the absorb tree (2026-11-05 - the compose receipt: absorb's latent_mma
fields drifted the hunks trailing context; the paged fields sit before
merge, the init calls after chunks_32_fp8, absorb's lines untouched). The
patch no longer applies standalone - the composed candidate is absorb +
marriage.

RE-ANCHORED onto v1.2.3+absorb (6ec5fa4cb + the re-anchored absorb),
2026-11-06: v1.2.3 consolidated the three inline latent.Table sites
(attend/blockLastRow/writeKeys) into the tables() helper - this port's
.logical = c.ls != 0 on t now lands there (one site; tk still defaults
false until the selist fix); the LatentShape guards moved into the helper
by the refactor and are preserved. cuda_native.zig's explain() table
re-anchored (v1.2.3 dropped GlmSoloWithDrafter and added BadCopyPolicy/
GlmKvHostNeedsPages; BadKvPages + PoolTooSmall still insert after
Fp8OnPages). cuda_glue.zig applies verbatim (the file is unchanged
between v1.2.2 and v1.2.3). NOTE: v1.2.3 threads tk into blockLastRow's
indexUpdate and attendLastRow's selectTokensProfile - with the selist fix
below, the MTP prompt-chunk path is covered too.

REBASE (2026-11-07, onto v1.2.4 267c5af6a): the snapshot tests append after the
KV_SHARE adapter test v1.2.4 added; the glm_kv_paged_records import sits beside the
pages family in the registry; the BadKvPages/PoolTooSmall explain lines, the
Pages.waiting field and the test-glm-kv-pages-host step re-anchored.

